---
description: Zustand Selectors: React Compiler-Friendly Rules
globs: packages/**/src/**/*.ts,packages/**/src/**/*.tsx
---
- Use split selectors: `store((s) => s.slice)` instead of aggregated object-shaped selectors.
- If you need multiple values, prefer a single array tuple selector with a fixed shape: `store((s) => [s.a, s.b] as const)`.
- Hoist selector lambdas to top-level whenever possible to avoid recreating functions each render.

## Avoid

- Returning new objects in selectors (e.g., `{ a: s.a, b: s.b }`) – this triggers identity churn and cache arity changes.
- Using `shallow` to mask churn; instead, return primitives/tuples and let equality be trivial.

